{
  "$comment": "Golden cases for the MFC re-import (import.proto) and for an import write crossing a client's own edit (sync.proto rule 6, IMPORT CROSSINGS). Every implementation (fc-coordinator's import, fc-mobile's store and sync engine) must agree with every case. `crossings`: one facet K on one client whose device is devices.self; each step is a Delta event (take), a user edit (edit), a Push of the unpushed edits (push), the PushResult of the oldest pushed edit (answer) or the user's resolution (resolve), and `expect` is the client after it: the value shown, the pending import conflict (MFC's side) or null, and the unpushed edits. Values stand for K's own fields; null is a tombstone. `reimports`: one import over abstract ids (occ ids order by name; new:{k} is the copy minted at ordinal k), heads (survivors maps a merged head to its survivor) and values. A figure cell is {value, v, base, baseV}: v and baseV rank versions, and this import writes at 100. `expect` is the whole state after the import, the user-owned and origin keys it wrote, the conflicts pending, and the unresolved rows.",
